"""Confined differential check: pre ``f`` (base tree) against post ``f'`` (patched tree).

Host side: ``run_differential`` builds a kernel profile (both trees read-only and
ro-bound, scratch the only writable path, proposer paths absent from the ruleset)
and runs this same file as the *driver* under ``hlith.sandbox.run_confined``.

Driver (inside the profile):
  1. reads and removes its spec (the nonce never stays readable to target code);
  2. probes every proposer path from inside the profile; a path counts as
     unreadable only when the kernel answers EACCES/EPERM for a path the host
     saw as existing (a missing path is not proof, so it stays readable=True);
  3. derives Hypothesis strategies from annotations, defaults, literals in the
     target body and constants in the tests that reference the target;
  4. runs pinned inputs first, then Hypothesis, each call evaluated in two
     evaluator processes (one per tree) that are confined again with no
     writable path; outcomes cross back only as JSON (never pickled);
  5. runs impacted tests (tests referencing the target) on both trees;
  6. prints one result line prefixed with the nonce.

"held" here is bounded: it carries execution count, explored strategies and an
explicit unexplored scope. It never claims universal equivalence.
"""

